{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC1m2cqekFSAcfyStTxm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The O3 workspace API is `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps, groupProps)`, with `launchWorkspaceGroup2(groupName, groupProps)` for groups. Each prop argument is optional and nullable. A null prop means the caller doesn't care about that context, so it never conflicts. Two non-null props conflict only if they are not shallow-equal.\n\n**Opening a workspace (implementation)**\n\n`launchWorkspace2` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts:133-321`) runs these steps:\n1. It throws if the workspace isn't registered, isn't registered to a window, or its window isn't registered to a group.\n2. If a different group is open, or the same group has incompatible group props, it prompts `CLOSE_WORKSPACE_GROUP`. On confirm, it replaces the group and discards all windows, then opens the new window with the workspace as its root.\n3. If the workspace's window is already open:\n   - If the window props are compatible and the workspace is already open with compatible props, it restores the window if it is hidden or not the most recent, and returns `true`.\n   - If the window props are compatible but the workspace is open with incompatible props, it prompts `CLOSE_WORKSPACE`. On confirm, it drops that window and reopens it with only the requested workspace.\n   - If the window props are incompatible, it prompts `CLOSE_WINDOW` and reopens the window with only the requested workspace.\n4. If the group is `closable`, it prompts `CLOSE_OTHER_WINDOWS` and, on confirm, leaves only this window open.\n5. Otherwise it appends the new window to the open windows.\n\nThe helper `arePropsCompatible` (lines 333-339) implements the nullish-or-shallow-equal rule. The prompt types are in `PromptReason` (lines 341-345), and `showClosePrompt` (lines 363-382) renders the confirmation modal. I did not read the body of `promptForClosingWorkspaces`, so I have not confirmed exactly which workspaces it lists for implicit closes.\n\n**Opening a group (implementation)**\n\n`launchWorkspaceGroup2` (`workspace2.ts:32-63`) returns `true` as a no-op if the same group with compatible props is already open. If a different or incompatible group is open, it prompts (`CLOSE_WORKSPACE_GROUP`). On confirm, or when nothing was open, it sets the new group and clears the windows. `closeWorkspaceGroup2` (lines 74-96) is the explicit close path; it prompts only when windows are open, unless `discardUnsavedChanges` is set.\n\n**Documentation**\n\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/launchWorkspace2.md` (1-78) describes the same conflict rules: group prompt, window-props prompt, workspace-props prompt, and that the call never creates a child workspace.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/launchWorkspaceGroup2.md` (1-39) covers the group-level rule that only one group can be open at a time.\n- The JSDoc comments on the implementation (`workspace2.ts:19-31` and `98-122`) carry the same text.\n\n**Example caller**\n\n`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx:97` calls `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps)`. It omits group props.\n\nI used 6 of the 10 search calls and 3 of the 20 read calls. One of the search calls failed because I used the short repo name; I then looked up the correct name and it worked.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 133, \"endLine\": 321},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 32, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 74, \